    "The script requests only 16 CPUs (`--cpus-per-task=16`), but all of the NAMD application runs are configured to use 64 threads (`+p64`). This will cause severe oversubscription, with 64 threads competing for 16 CPU cores, which will lead to a significant performance degradation due to context switching. The number of CPUs requested should be increased to at least 64.",
    "The script hardcodes the GPU device to be used (`+devices 0`). This bypasses the scheduler's resource assignment and isolation mechanisms. Flux will allocate a specific physical GPU to the job and make it visible as device 0 through the `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` or `ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES` environment variables. While this may work for a single-GPU job, it is not a robust practice and can cause issues on multi-GPU nodes if a different physical device is assigned. The application should ideally be configured to use the GPU assigned by the scheduler automatically."
